---
import Layout from "../../Base.astro";
import SimpleHero from "../../components/SimpleHero.astro";
import FeaturedArticles from "../../components/FeaturedArticles.astro";
import "../../styles/pages/_services-list.scss";
---

<Layout
  title="AI Chatbots & Agents for Websites and Workflows | Kelp"
  description="Build AI chatbots and agents that answer real questions, use approved information, connect to your systems, and hand off to people when needed."
>
  <SimpleHero
    tagline="AI Services"
    title="AI Chatbots & Agents That Know Their Job"
    description="A useful chatbot does more than greet visitors. It helps someone find an answer, choose the right next step, or get a task moving. Kelp designs AI chatbots and agents around the questions people actually ask and the work your team needs done."
    lottieFile="ai-chatbots.json"
  />
  <section class="service-body">
    <div class="wrapper wrapper--narrow">
      <h2>Where Teams Get Stuck</h2>
      <p>
        Generic bots can sound confident while giving the wrong answer. They may
        know nothing about your policies, show the wrong product information, or
        collect a lead without enough context for your team to follow up. More
        capable agents introduce another question: what should they be allowed
        to do on a customer's behalf?
      </p>
      <h2>How We Fix It</h2>
      <p>
        We give each experience a defined role. A website assistant may answer
        common service questions and guide a visitor to the right page. A
        commerce assistant may help compare products using current catalog
        information. An internal agent may prepare a summary or a draft for a
        staff member to review. We separate answers from actions and set
        permissions accordingly.
      </p>
      <h2>Start with Approved Knowledge</h2>
      <p>
        The bot needs a dependable source: service details, product
        specifications, policies, help content, or internal documents that your
        team has approved. We organize that information, decide how it stays
        current, and make it clear when the bot does not have enough to answer.
        Good source material matters more than a clever opening message.
      </p>
      <h2>Give People a Clear Handoff</h2>
      <p>
        Some questions need a person. We design handoffs for uncertain answers,
        sensitive situations, custom quotes, and requests outside the bot's
        scope. When a human takes over, they should receive useful context
        rather than asking the visitor to start again. Any agent action, such as
        creating a record or starting a workflow, needs a clear permission and
        review rule.
      </p>
      <h2>Keep Improving After Launch</h2>
      <p>
        We review the questions people ask, where the bot helps, where it fails,
        and whether it leads to useful outcomes. The content, prompts, and
        connected workflows can then improve with real usage. Kelp can also
        connect the experience to your website and the systems that support it.
      </p>
      <h2>What the Work Includes</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Conversation goals and customer-question research</li>
        <li>Approved knowledge and content planning</li>
        <li>Chatbot or agent design and development</li>
        <li>System connections, permissions, and human handoffs</li>
        <li>Quality review, measurement, and ongoing refinement</li>
      </ul>
      <h2>What Moving Forward Looks Like</h2>
      <p>
        Tell us the questions your team answers again and again, along with the
        actions a visitor or staff member might need next. We can recommend
        where a chatbot, an agent, or a simpler website improvement would help
        most. Talk with Kelp about the use case.
      </p>
      <h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
      <h3 class="h4">Can an AI agent take actions in our systems?</h3>
      <p>
        It can be designed to, when the connected system supports the action and
        the permissions are clear. We start with a narrow task and decide which
        actions require a person's approval.
      </p>
      <p>
        <a href="/contact/" class="button button--green">
          Talk Through Your Project
        </a>
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
  <FeaturedArticles />
</Layout>
